 R←TestReport;m;b;same;capture;cases;c;book;modern;stamp;sky;ts;parts;lines
⍝ The printed report is character-for-character the book's.
⍝ Both versions are run in a child Dyalog by test/report.apls, so that
⍝ each prints through ⎕← at the same ⎕PW, folding long lines alike.
⍝ The GENERATED line holds the time of printing and is checked
⍝ separately against Printed with a fixed timestamp.
 m←## ⋄ b←##.Data ⋄ R←1
 same←{(⊃⍵)≡2⊃⍵:1 ⋄ 0⊣⎕←'FAIL: TestReport: ',⍺}

⍝ capture version width observation → printed lines (empty lines kept)
 capture←{
     cmd←'REPORT_VERSION=',⍺,' REPORT_PW=',(⍕⊃⍵),' REPORT_OBS=''',(⍕2⊃⍵),''''
     t←'UTF-8'⎕UCS ⎕UCS∊(⎕SH cmd,' dyalog -script test/report.apls'),¨⎕UCS 10
     t←(⎕UCS 10)@{⍵=⎕UCS 13}t
     {1↓¨(⍵=⎕UCS 10)⊂⍵}(⎕UCS 10),t
 }
 stamp←{'GENERATED '≡10↑⍵}¨

⍝ width (month day year hour lat long): Anaheim 1974 at several widths
⍝ either side of the two-column threshold (100); Kohoutek in range;
⍝ southern hemisphere
 cases←(80(5 16 1974 5 33.767 ¯117.833))(99(5 16 1974 5 33.767 ¯117.833))
 cases,←(100(5 16 1974 5 33.767 ¯117.833))(120(5 16 1974 5 33.767 ¯117.833))
 cases,←(80(1 10 1974 18 51.5 ¯0.13))(120(12 25 1975 10 ¯33.87 151.21))
 :For c :In cases
     book←'book'capture c
     modern←'modern'capture c
     R∧←('one GENERATED line, book ',⍕c)same 1(+/stamp book)
     R∧←('one GENERATED line, modern ',⍕c)same 1(+/stamp modern)
     R∧←('report ',⍕c)same((~stamp book)/book)((~stamp modern)/modern)
 :EndFor

⍝ Printed: the book's footer for a given timestamp; as in the book, the
⍝ day name is the observation's, not the timestamp's (#22)
 sky←m.SkyAt(b.JNU 5 16 1974)5 33.767 ¯117.833
 R∧←'Printed afternoon'same(''  'GENERATED THURSDAY 2026/10/11 AT 3:07 PM')(2026 10 11 15 7 30 0 m.Printed sky)
 R∧←'Printed midnight hour'same('' 'GENERATED THURSDAY 2026/1/2 AT 12:05 AM')(2026 1 2 0 5 0 0 m.Printed sky)

⍝ Work: the parts in the book's order, each a vector of lines
 ts←2026 10 11 15 7 30 0
 parts←(m.Caption sky)(80 m.ReportPlanets sky)(80 m.PlotStars sky)(80 m.ReportStars sky)(ts m.Printed sky)
 lines←{(1=≢⍴⍵)∧0∧.=80|⎕DR¨⍵}                ⍝ a vector of character arrays
 R∧←'parts are vectors of lines'same 1(∧/lines¨parts)
 R∧←'Work'same(⊃,/parts)(80 ts m.Work sky)

 :If R
     ⎕←'PASS: TestReport (',(⍕≢cases),' reports)'
 :EndIf
